{{- /* Which Proton Pass vault this machine's secrets live in.

       One name per role, and they are separate vaults rather than one shared
       one on purpose: a work machine holding the personal signing key, ssh
       auth key and gh token is the thing the split exists to prevent, and
       "same vault, different items" would not prevent it — a vault-scoped PAT
       reads all of it.

       Read two ways, which is why it is a template rather than a constant:
       templates call it directly, and dot_config/dotfiles/machine.env.tmpl
       renders it into a file the plain scripts source, since three of the four
       vault consumers are not templates. */ -}}
{{- if contains " work " (includeTemplate "profiles" .) -}}
Work
{{- else -}}
Dotfiles
{{- end -}}
